    content: `<h2>What Is Spy Mode?</h2><p>Spy Mode is one of MiloBolo's most unique features, inspired by Omegle's original question mode. It allows for a three-person interaction with distinct roles: the Spy (question asker), Stranger 1, and Stranger 2.</p><h2>How to Be the Spy</h2><p>Navigate to /spy or click "Spy / Question Mode" from the homepage. You will see a text field where you can type your question. You can also choose from sample questions like "Is social media making people more lonely?" Once you submit, MiloBolo pairs two strangers to discuss your question while you watch.</p><h2>What Spies Can and Cannot Do</h2><p>As a spy, you can read the entire conversation in real time. You cannot send messages — you are a silent observer. You can disconnect at any time without affecting the strangers' conversation.</p><h2>How to Be a Stranger</h2><p>Click "Join as a Stranger" and you will be matched with another stranger and given a question to discuss. You and the other stranger can chat freely while a spy watches silently.</p><h2>Best Questions to Ask</h2><p>The best Spy Mode questions are open-ended and slightly controversial — not offensive, but thought-provoking. Questions about life choices, hypotheticals, and social issues tend to generate the most engaging discussions.</p><h2>Sample Questions</h2><ul><li>Would you rather be rich and miserable or poor and happy?</li><li>Is technology making humans more or less creative?</li><li>What is more important — intelligence or kindness?</li></ul>`,
