    category: "How-To Guides", tags: ["voice call","text chat","features","audio"], date: "2025-05-18", readTime: 3,
    content: `<h2>Voice in Text Mode</h2><p>MiloBolo's text chat mode does not require a camera — but it does optionally support voice calls. This is perfect if you want audio conversation without video.</p><h2>How to Start a Voice Call</h2><p>During an active text chat session, look for the Phone icon in the chat panel toolbar. Click it to initiate a voice call with your current stranger. The stranger will be notified and their browser will ask for microphone permission.</p><h2>What Happens During a Voice Call</h2><p>If both users have microphone access, a peer-to-peer audio connection is established. This connection is direct — your audio goes browser-to-browser without passing through MiloBolo's servers. You can continue typing in the chat while talking.</p><h2>How to End the Call</h2><p>Click the Phone End icon to terminate the voice connection. The text chat continues normally after.</p><h2>Privacy Note</h2><p>Voice calls use WebRTC, the same peer-to-peer technology used for video. Your IP address is shared with your conversation partner's browser during the call — this is a technical requirement of WebRTC. If this concerns you, use text-only mode.</p>`,
