    category: "How-To Guides", tags: ["PWA","install","app","mobile"], date: "2025-04-20", readTime: 4,
    content: `<h2>What Is a PWA?</h2><p>A Progressive Web App (PWA) is a website that can be installed on your device like a native app. It works offline for some features, launches from your home screen, and runs in its own window without browser chrome.</p><h2>Install on Android (Chrome)</h2><p>Open MiloBolo in Chrome. Tap the three-dot menu in the top right. Select "Add to Home Screen" or "Install App". Tap Install in the confirmation dialog. MiloBolo will appear on your home screen and in your app drawer.</p><h2>Install on iPhone / iPad (Safari)</h2><p>Open MiloBolo in Safari. Tap the Share button (box with arrow). Scroll down and tap "Add to Home Screen". Tap Add in the top right. MiloBolo will appear on your home screen.</p><h2>Install on Desktop (Chrome/Edge)</h2><p>Look for the install icon (computer with download arrow) in your browser's address bar. Click it and then click Install. MiloBolo will open in its own window, separate from your browser.</p><h2>Benefits of the PWA</h2><ul><li>Faster loading with cached assets</li><li>App icon on home screen for quick access</li><li>Full-screen mode without browser bars</li><li>Push notification support (optional)</li></ul>`,
