    title: "How MiloBolo Responds to Data Breaches and Security Incidents",
    excerpt: "MiloBolo's data breach response process, notification timeline, and how we protect you if an incident occurs.",
    category: "Privacy", tags: ["data breach","security","incident response","transparency"], date: "2025-04-14", readTime: 4,
    content: `<h2>Our Commitment to Transparency</h2><p>If a security incident occurs affecting user data, MiloBolo commits to transparent and prompt notification. Here is our response process.</p><h2>Detection and Assessment</h2><p>Our monitoring systems are configured to detect unusual access patterns. If a potential breach is detected, our security team assesses scope and impact within 24 hours.</p><h2>Notification Timeline</h2><p>Under GDPR, we are required to notify relevant supervisory authorities within 72 hours of becoming aware of a breach affecting EU/UK users. Affected users are notified without undue delay via email if their account data is affected.</p><h2>What We Notify You About</h2><p>Our notification will clearly describe: what data was affected, when the incident occurred, what we have done to contain it, and what steps you should take (e.g., changing passwords).</p><h2>Why Breach Impact Is Limited</h2><p>Because MiloBolo stores so little data, the impact of any breach is inherently limited. No message content, no video, no audio is ever stored. A breach of our database would expose only account metadata — display names, email addresses, and session statistics.</p>`,
