    category: "Features", tags: ["chat history","features","account","privacy"], date: "2025-05-31", readTime: 4,
    content: `<h2>Optional, Private, Your Choice</h2><p>MiloBolo does not store chat messages — but for registered users, we can record session metadata: when you chatted, for how long, how many messages you exchanged, and which interest you matched on. Message content is never stored.</p><h2>How to Enable Chat History</h2><p>Chat history requires a MiloBolo account. Once registered, go to your profile settings and enable "Save chat history". From that point, each session's metadata will be recorded.</p><h2>Viewing Your History</h2><p>Navigate to /history to see your session list. Each entry shows date, duration, mode, message count, and matched interest if applicable. You cannot view message content because it is never stored.</p><h2>How to Disable or Delete</h2><p>You can disable history recording or delete all historical records from your profile settings at any time. Deletion is immediate and permanent.</p><h2>Privacy Note</h2><p>Your chat history is private — only you can see it. It is protected by Supabase Row-Level Security, which means our database cannot return your history to any other user even with a direct query.</p>`,
