    category: "Features", tags: ["features","online counter","matchmaking","real-time"], date: "2025-05-24", readTime: 3,
    content: `<h2>Knowing Who Is There</h2><p>The online counter in MiloBolo's header shows approximately how many users are currently connected to the platform. This is not just a decorative feature — it directly affects your experience.</p><h2>How It Is Calculated</h2><p>The counter reflects the number of active Socket.IO connections to MiloBolo's signaling server. It updates every 10 seconds via a lightweight REST API call. The counter is approximate — users who have navigated away without closing the tab may still be counted for a brief period.</p><h2>What It Means for Matchmaking</h2><p>More users online means faster matching. If the counter is high, you will typically be matched within 1-3 seconds. If it is lower, matching may take 10-30 seconds before falling back to a global queue.</p><h2>Technical Note</h2><p>MiloBolo uses REST polling for the counter rather than a persistent Socket.IO connection. This prevents spurious WebSocket connections on pages where you are not actively chatting, reducing server load and browser resource usage.</p>`,
